Z||000002||Oreif||02-08-2001||04:22 PM||||PBS, There is no need for you to apologize. We all suspected he was a little slow to begin with. At least it didn't cause both forums to flood/flame each other. I think he's gone for good.<P>BTW ~ I saw your website with the front mounted sub. My question is do you just fire it in the front or did you duct it into the passenger compartment? I am writing an article for our club newsletter about stereo installations and since an MR2 has the same "lack" of space as a Fiero for large subs, I was curious how you did it and how it sounds. Also, I have never seen the uderside of an MR2 but was curious how the front firewall meets the trunk. I noticed in your pics the spare tire is mounted towards the passenger compartment. Does that wall go all the way down to the floor?<BR>Thanks,<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||02-08-2001||04:30 PM||||NO PROBLEM DAN<BR> I think were all in agreement here that hes an idiot. enough said.<P>Roger||||reg||1
Z||000004||PearlBlueSoul||02-08-2001||04:31 PM||||alright, about the sub.  <P>I had a 12" in a normal truck box I merely sat in the trunk.  sealed box, no ports into the cabin.  Sounded 100% fine, and made a GREAT balance in sound.  My dad's a pro sound studio designer, and was also suprised it sounded so good (if that says anything for merit).  I ran a wire through an existing grommet and it worked just fine.  The firewall is about a foot high, and splits off as the rack/pinion is stuffed below and in between the passenger compartment and the front trunk firewall.  I'll see if I can get my webcam, pull out the spare and show you what one of our trunks looks like on the empty side.  This should be easy seeing as I no longer have my sub (gave it to my sister as a b-day present.  Don't worry, I'm devising a way to stuff in 2 10"s within the next few months.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I'll be sure to let you know how that one goes).  <P>The spare tire in our cars are mounted towards the passenger compartment, yes, and that leaves about 6-8" of trunk floor you can see.  it doesn't tilt in that much at all (unless you have a full size spare in which case there's no chance of a sub fitting in there w/o a very thin box and a sub that isn't that deep).  Again, I'll see about pics today.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||02-08-2001||04:40 PM||||LMAO!! hehe only on this board can a post go from an apology to a discussion on subs! hehehe I LOVE IT!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P><BR>where you been dan.. haven't seen you out on barret pkwy. latley... ||||reg||1
Z||000006||ArmandoP||02-08-2001||04:46 PM||||I can vouch for the sound of the sub up front.... WOW!<BR>Ive been in two MKI's that have this setup, and the sound is surprisingly good, with no noticable rattle whatsoever....<BR>as far as MR-BAD/mr2 and fiero owner...he's a joke...just ignore him if he comes back on here...we try to ignore him over there, but he just keeps coming back. oh well.<BR>Armando<P>------------------<BR>__________________<BR>will work for MR2 parts!!! <BR>1987 MR2 NA t-bar csp with 700 miles on its new engine. <BR>TRD copper head gasket, milled head .020, 2 short shifters,metal masters rear brake pads, 195-60-14 (soon to get new tires), clear corners, Clevite 77 bearings, NO A/C, MAF relocation mod, red silicon vacuum hoses, redline tranny fluid,and the stock exhaust with a WHOLE bunch of broken welds! <BR>indiana/illinois MR2 owners club<BR>[URLhttp://php.indiana.edu/~ajperez/inimoc.html[/URL]<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://php.indiana.edu/~ajperez/mytwo.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||PearlBlueSoul||02-08-2001||04:59 PM||||Ok, I've got some pictures taken for you.  Blame the focus of the pictures on yours truly.  I was on my laptop and the sun was out, couldn't tell it was out of focus till after I came inside and looked at them.  oh well. you'll see what I mean regardles.<P>soon as I get them up on my server I'll edit this post and let ya know.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||10
Z||000008||PearlBlueSoul||02-08-2001||05:03 PM||||Oh, 1FSTM6, you didn't know?  My car is OOC due to a bad trans.  1st/2nd gear synchro took a hike on me about 3-4 weeks ago.  I'm missing my 2 forward gears at the moment, and in the process of looking into getting a used trans.  only have 100 bucks to play with.    What's worse is that not but a week before the trans blew I hit my sister's car.  still is bent up, right rear quarter panel.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  I've just got the worst luck with cars, it's not even funny.  if it's not wrecked, it blows up.  and sometimes both at once. <P>Think Ed at Engineered would let me snag a lift for a while to stuff in another trans?  its no big deal if he can't, I'll do it at home with the good 'ol jacks and stands.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||PearlBlueSoul||02-08-2001||05:52 PM||||OK, these pics are named in reverse order of how I took them. <P>Pics 1-3 show me in the trunk<BR>pics 4-about 5-6 show the trunk completely empty and stripped of it's plastic.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Notice the "shelf" that extends out where hoses go through in the back of the trunk.  That shelf has the steering rack beneath it, and there's no firewall after that.  it's seperate trunk well and passenger footwell.  <BR>Pics 5/6-10 are of the trunk with the spare tire in there, as well as the plastic.  it's a fairly spacious trunk, with ample room for a box.  I'd estimate around 1-2' deep, (looking straight into the trunk) 1-2' in vertical, and about 5-6' horizontal space.  <BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/poniepearl/trunk1.JPG" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/poniepearl/trunk1.JPG</A>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/poniepearl/trunk2.JPG" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/poniepearl/trunk2.JPG</A>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/poniepearl/trunk3.JPG" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/poniepearl/trunk3.JPG</A>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/poniepearl/trunk4.JPG" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/poniepearl/trunk4.JPG</A>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/poniepearl/trunk5.JPG" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/poniepearl/trunk5.JPG</A>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/poniepearl/trunk6.JPG" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/poniepearl/trunk6.JPG</A>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/poniepearl/trunk7.JPG" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/poniepearl/trunk7.JPG</A>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/poniepearl/trunk8.JPG" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/poniepearl/trunk8.JPG</A>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/poniepearl/trunk9.JPG" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/poniepearl/trunk9.JPG</A>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/poniepearl/trunk10.JPG" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/poniepearl/trunk10.JPG</A> ||||reg||1
